<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-PNG wants to hire stock exchange CEO.</title>
<headline>RTRS-PNG wants to hire stock exchange CEO.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Papua New Guinea on Friday placed an advertisement seeking a chief executive officer for its embryonic national stock exchange.</p>
<p>The advertisment in the Australian Financial Review newspaper said the exchange would become operational during 1997.</p>
<p>It said the successful candidate would work in an &quot;unusual and challenging environment&quot; and could be someone who is &quot;seeking career development opportunities or more mature persons, recently retired or nearing retirement&quot;.  </p>
<p>The interview process was being overseen by former Australian Stock Exchange official Peter Marshman who was advising the PNG government on the establishment of the stock exchange.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
